UnitMovementMng is the sole mutator for where units sit on the map, how they stack on a tile, and how they chain into move-as-one groups. Bind the live game state once at setup, and load movement costs from statics before any step queries; without that, cost and step checks are not meaningful. New units enter the world either by placing a typed unit onto a friendly or empty tile, or by finishing a spawn that already owns a pool slot and only needs owner, movement points, and map attachment. Stacks are co-located allies on one tile who still move independently; groups are a head with real coordinates plus followers that clear their own coordinates and hang only off the group link, so they travel when the head does.

Day-to-day movement is always one orthogonal or diagonal step at a time: ask whether the key (always the group head if there is a group) can enter the destination under domain, alliance, and movement-point rules, then apply the step to unlink from the old tile, append on the new one, and debit the group’s shared budget. Building or breaking groups uses the link and unlink helpers so followers leave the tile stack and only the head remains map-visible. Higher-level helpers exist for AI flows that peel a departing force while leaving a fixed defense count behind, for destroying a unit cleanly from both axes, and for splitting a group roughly in half by type when an assault needs an occupy column and a remainder. Prefer these entry points over writing tile heads or link fields by hand; the cohesion validator exists because hand-edits are easy to get wrong.
